# Copy to .env.test.local and fill in from a DEDICATED test Supabase project
# — never the project your .env.local points at. These tests create real
# throwaway auth users, groups, expenses and settlements; running them
# against a project you actually use will pollute it with test data.
#
# Project Settings -> API on the test project:
SUPABASE_TEST_URL=https://YOUR_TEST_PROJECT_REF.supabase.co
SUPABASE_TEST_ANON_KEY=your-test-project-anon-key

# Project Settings -> API -> service_role (secret). Only ever used by
# tests/rls/helpers.ts for privileged fixture seeding, never sent to a
# browser. This file is gitignored — never commit a real key.
SUPABASE_TEST_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=your-test-project-service-role-key
